Two owner rulings from the same evening, plus a correction to something the
ADR said twice.

§13 — confidence is not arbitrated by precedence. Measured on the 92 agreed
edges: tree-sitter calls carry 0.4–0.85 evidence_derived, SCIP references a
uniform 0.85 emitter_constant. Incumbent-first would leave an edge the
type-aware backend just confirmed at 0.5, inverting ADR-0012's premise that
confirmation upgrades. Three cases: sole producer keeps its value; same
pathway twice is not new evidence (precedence); distinct pathways for one
(src, dst, edge_type) yield a DECLARED corroboration level — built-in 0.95,
ADR-0012's own number, configurable in the §5 table — with a new
confidence_source value `corroborated` and CONFIDENCE_MODEL v2.0 → v2.1.
Not max (returns the constant), not noisy-OR (the producers read the same
text; it would push everything to ≈0.98).

§14 — a resolved first-party edge demotes a same-(src, line) external-stub
edge by rank_score (ADR-0039 ruling 3), stamped on the stub as a positive
claim naming the superseding edge, never deleted. 33 of 257 stub sites on
the measured crate, an upper bound until the implementing row separates
same-call from co-located reference.

Correction: §1 and §6 cited confidence_source=composite as the precedent
for multi-producer provenance. ADR-0039 defines composite as transitional
blended ranking slated for elimination, and nothing produces it. The
precedent is the FIELD, not that value; reusing the value would be a
conceptual leak. §4 now admits combining rules for numeric attributes; §5
scopes incumbent-first to categorical ones.

Tracker: WI-lihis filed for §14 (blocked by WI-kokiz); §13 noted on
WI-binis; WI-gapup widened to enum variants (9 of 9 pair SCIP class against
tree-sitter field on the same artifact).

